      non-commercial purposes. (use by or within a for-profit company, including its internal research and development, is commercial use; see Section 3)
   c. You may modify the code internally, for your own research within
      your organization. Internal modification requires no permission.

2. Restrictions
   a. You may not redistribute the code -- original or modified, in
      whole or in part, including public forks or mirrors -- without
      prior written permission of the copyright holder.
   b. You may not distribute or publish modified versions. Internal
      modification is permitted; making a modified version available
      to others is not.
   c. You may not use TENRYU commercially -- including in paid services, consulting deliverables, products, or internal research and development at a for-profit company -- without a
      fee-based license agreement with the copyright holder.

3. Commercial licensing
   Commercial use includes use by or within a for-profit entity, including its internal research and development.
   Commercial use requires a fee-based license agreement. Contact the
   developer in advance through the TENRYU GitHub repository (Issues)
   to arrange terms.

4. Citation
   If TENRYU contributes to published work, please acknowledge it,
   e.g.: "This work used the TENRYU radiation-hydrodynamics code
   developed by Ryunosuke Takizawa (Institute of Laser Engineering,
   The University of Osaka)."

